          %title Partial equivalence relations
          %h1#partial_equivalence_relations Partial equivalence relations
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#category_of_pers_and_interpretation_of_the_polymorphic_lambda_calculus"} Category of PERs and interpretation of the polymorphic lambda calculus
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            A
            %strong partial equivalence relation
            (sometimes abbreviated
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong PER
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
            satisfying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+relation"} symmetry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitivity
            conditions of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexivity
            condition. That is, a partial equivalence relation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a binary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y) \subseteq X^2
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y)
            implies
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(y, x)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, y)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(y, z)
            together imply
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, z)
          %p
            Just as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unary+relations"} unary relations
            on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and equivalence relations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotients
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            correspond to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotients"} subquotients
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(x, x)
            comprise a subset of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Consider the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequences"} infinite sequences
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            be related if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{i,j\to \infty} {|x_i - y_j|} = 0 .
          %p
            Then this defines a partial equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+real+numbers"} Cauchy real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+sequences"} Cauchy sequences
            of rational numbers (under the absolute-value metric), and then we impose a total equivalence relation on the Cauchy sequences. But a single partial equivalence relation does all of the work. (This example generalises in the usual ways.)
          %h2#category_of_pers_and_interpretation_of_the_polymorphic_lambda_calculus Category of PERs and interpretation of the polymorphic lambda calculus
          %p
            We can form
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+PERs"} categories of PERs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            from a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tripos"} tripos
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} partial combinatory algebra
            is a model of combinatory logic (or, roughly speaking, the untyped lambda calculus). If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a partial combinatory algebra, then the partial equivalence relations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are the objects of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+PERs"} category of PERs
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/assemblies"} assemblies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
          %p
            In more detail, consider the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory#typeforming_rules"} type forming rules
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo :
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi X
                  %mo .
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma,\tau ::= X | \sigma\to \tau | \forall X.\sigma
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            ranges over type variables.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Closed types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                (i.e. those with no free variables) are interpreted as PERs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llbracket{\tau}\rrbracket
                over the fixed partial combinatory algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                Open types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                type variables are interpreted as assignments from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                PERs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 1
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_1\dots R_n
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to a PER
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi τ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mn 1
                          %mi …
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llbracket{\tau}\rrbracket_{R_1\dots R_n}
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"}> Function types
                  \:
                If the closed types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                are interpreted as PERs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi σ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llbracket \sigma\rrbracket
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llbracket \tau\rrbracket
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo →
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma\to\tau
                is interpreted as the PER
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                        %mi σ
                        %mo →
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \llbracket \sigma\to\tau\rrbracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo .
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a\in A | \forall b\in A.\ b\in\dom(\llbracket \sigma\rrbracket) \implies a\cdot b\in \dom(\llbracket \tau\rrbracket)\}
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                  %mi σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,a')\in \llbracket \sigma\to\tau\rrbracket
            if for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b,b')\in \llbracket \sigma\rrbracket
            we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a\cdot b,a'\cdot b')\in \llbracket \tau\rrbracket
          %p For open types, the definition is similar, just parameterize by the interpretation of the type variables.
          %ul
            %li
              %em Polymorphic types:
              If the type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              has one free type variable,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi X
                      %mo .
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtext a PER
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟦
                      %mi τ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⟧
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\llbracket \forall X.\tau\rrbracket =
                      \\bigcap_{R\ \text{ a PER}} \llbracket \tau\rrbracket_R
              %p For types with more free variables, the definition is similar, just parameterize by the interpretation of the type variables.
